(2. Experiment 1: Verification of Newton Second Law \(F = ma\)) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
0 -14 Td
(Apparatus: Low-friction air track, glider, hanging weight carrier, photogates, digital timer.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
0 -14 Td
(Theory: Newton second law states that net force equals mass multiplied by acceleration.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
0 -14 Td
(Procedure: Vary hanging mass m_h while keeping total system mass constant. Measure acceleration) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
0 -14 Td
(using dual infrared photogates across 0.50m and 1.00m distance markers.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
0 -14 Td
(Analysis: Plot Net Force vs Acceleration. The slope represents experimental system mass.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
0 -10 Td
